while (true)
{
    var results = await client.GetReadResultAsync(operationId);

    if (results.Status == OperationStatusCodes.Succeeded)
    {
        // Process the results
        break;
    }
    else if (results.Status == OperationStatusCodes.Failed)
    {
        // Handle failure
        break;
    }

    // Delay to avoid hammering the service with requests
    await Task.Delay(1000);
}

You need to ensure that the read operation has completed successfully before proceeding. Checking the status value ensures the operation has finished.

Repeatedly checking the status of the read operation until it is complete allows you to handle the asynchronous nature of the operation correctly

